Translation patch: RISTRETTO_BASEPOINT_TABLE (src/constants.rs)

Change: the pointer cast
`&*(ED25519_BASEPOINT_TABLE as *const EdwardsBasepointTable as *const RistrettoBasepointTable)`
(in an `unsafe` block) becomes
`&RistrettoBasepointTable(EdwardsBasepointTable(ED25519_BASEPOINT_TABLE.0))`, i.e. the
static is built by copying the table's `Copy` array of lookup tables into a new
`RistrettoBasepointTable` instead of reinterpreting the pointer to the Ed25519 table.

Why: Charon turns the cast into a raw borrow (`&raw const`), which Aeneas rejects
("Unsupported operation"), so the original could only be translated as opaque.

Behaviour: same value, different memory. `RistrettoBasepointTable` is a
`#[repr(transparent)]` wrapper of `EdwardsBasepointTable`, so the copy holds exactly the
same table entries and every multiplication through it reads the same data and returns
the same result. The difference: the binary holds a second copy of the table data
(about 30 KB) and `RISTRETTO_BASEPOINT_TABLE.0` no longer has the same address as
`*ED25519_BASEPOINT_TABLE`; nothing in the crate compares these addresses.
(Context is plain rather than `-W`: a `static` has no function boundary, so `-W` would
include the whole file above it.)

Remove this patch when Aeneas translates the original code: delete the file, add the
static back to `opaque` in Cargo.toml if needed, run ./scripts/aeneas-translate.sh and
`lake build`, and check both succeed.

diff --git a/curve25519-dalek/src/constants.rs b/curve25519-dalek/src/constants.rs
index 6f5ffa8..0172ac5 100644
--- a/curve25519-dalek/src/constants.rs
+++ b/curve25519-dalek/src/constants.rs
@@ -79,17 +79,14 @@
 
 #[cfg(feature = "precomputed-tables")]
 use crate::ristretto::RistrettoBasepointTable;
 
 /// The Ristretto basepoint, as a `RistrettoBasepointTable` for scalar multiplication.
 #[cfg(feature = "precomputed-tables")]
-pub static RISTRETTO_BASEPOINT_TABLE: &RistrettoBasepointTable = unsafe {
-    // SAFETY: `RistrettoBasepointTable` is a `#[repr(transparent)]` newtype of
-    // `EdwardsBasepointTable`
-    &*(ED25519_BASEPOINT_TABLE as *const EdwardsBasepointTable as *const RistrettoBasepointTable)
-};
+pub static RISTRETTO_BASEPOINT_TABLE: &RistrettoBasepointTable =
+    &RistrettoBasepointTable(EdwardsBasepointTable(ED25519_BASEPOINT_TABLE.0));
 
